  "notes": "USAGE:\n{記名|きめい} is a compound of {記|き} (to record) and {名|めい} (name). It simply means that a name is written down, as opposed to being anonymous.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {署名|しょめい} — a signature (the act of signing one's name as authentication)\n- {記名|きめい} — writing one's name (not necessarily as a signature or legal act)\n- {無記名|むきめい} — anonymous, unnamed (the opposite: {無記名|むきめい}{投票|とうひょう} = secret ballot)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {記名|きめい}{投票|とうひょう} (signed/open ballot)\n- {無記名|むきめい}{投票|とうひょう} (secret/anonymous ballot)\n- {記名|きめい}{式|しき} (signed/named format)\n- {記名|きめい}する (write one's name)",
